{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the sons of Cush: Seba and Havilah</b> — these were heads of nations, and the sons of Raamah were two peoples. But Nimrod was not a nation; therefore Scripture wrote afterward, \"And Cush begot Nimrod\" and did not say, \"And the sons of Cush: Nimrod and Seba and Havilah.\" But Put was a single nation and did not produce distinct nations like Egypt and Canaan; therefore Scripture did not bring him back (i.e., did not enumerate his descendants). And in Bereshit Rabbah (Genesis Rabbah 37:2), Resh Lakish said: We were of the opinion that the family of Put was swallowed up, and Ezekiel came and explained, \"Put and Lud and all the mixed rabble\" (Ezekiel 30:5) — for because Scripture did not bring him back, we were of the opinion that his seed intermingled among the sons of Canaan, and they were not a nation and did not inherit for themselves a land that would be called by their name. But also regarding Magog and Madai and Tubal and Meshech and Tiras, the sons of Japheth, he did not mention families in their generations, and likewise with the sons of Shem — Elam and Asshur and Arpachshad and Lud — they were heads of nations and he did not mention generations for them, for each one was a single nation in its land and did not beget distinct nations."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:26:55.691610305Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}